# Asset Vault — Frontend Environment Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.

# ============================================
# REQUIRED
# ============================================

# Backend API base URL.
#   Development: http://localhost:3000/api/v1
#   Production:  https://your-domain.com/api/v1
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1

# Clerk publishable key. The app WILL NOT START without this — main.tsx renders a
# configuration error screen instead of the UI. Create an application at
# https://dashboard.clerk.com and copy its publishable key (it begins with pk_test_
# for development instances, pk_live_ for production).
# This key is public by design and is safe to ship in the client bundle; the secret
# key belongs in the backend environment, never here.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_replace_me

# ============================================
# PRODUCTION NOTES
# ============================================
# 1. Point VITE_API_BASE_URL at your production backend.
# 2. Allow your frontend origin in the backend's CORS configuration.
# 3. Never commit the real .env — only this example belongs in git.
# 4. Vite inlines these at BUILD time, so rebuild after changing them; restarting
#    the dev server is not enough for a production bundle.
